From cb1721af2365e9ae047b7c4e7e8062b434d82f81 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: r-vdp <ramses@well-founded.dev>
Date: Thu, 9 Apr 2026 19:40:36 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] nixos-subids: init at 0.1.0

Maintains /etc/subuid and /etc/subgid from declarative
users.users.<name>.{autoSubUidGidRange,subUidRanges,subGidRanges} when
user management is handled by userborn or systemd-sysusers.

Unlike the perl allocator, ranges are checked for overlap across owners
and auto-allocated ranges skip explicitly claimed intervals (like the
1e9 root range that the incus module sets). Existing entries are
never removed so a range can never be reassigned to a different owner.

Files are written atomically as regular files; newuidmap from
shadow-utils opens them with O_NOFOLLOW so a symlink would not work.

See: https://github.com/nikstur/userborn/issues/7
